  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I just bumped in a very small API/SDK bug. SDK is version 3.2.3.\n\nAt begin of first upload i made text in description. When i upload later again updated world, i noticed the words in description are messed up. Spaces are moved up, some extra characters added. I have never seen it. See the screenshots.\n\nI tried to replace the faulty description with correct text. Same text as before. But it refuses to update it. When i tried to change it too on website, it returned with exact same messed up text. So it's clearly sort of API bug.\n\nThen i give up after many tries to restore it, i decide to type different text, with some words changed. Suddenly it accept the new text and not more messed text as result.\n\nIt seems there is some check there that reject the \"new\" text because it's exact same string - but only at database level - check and not check at website / sdk side. The API still returns the wrong text for some reason. Did i found very small bug in API system?\n\nAnyway, there is small chance the text will messed up by new uploads with exact same text in SDK. Cannot repeat it easy, but what happened earlier was annoying bug. Then you cannot restore it with exact same text replacement. You must type updated text, different from earlier text, then the messed up text will replaced correctly.",
